# Build-time configuration for the deployed front end.
#
# Copy to app/.env.production and fill in. Vite reads it automatically during
# `bun run build`, and **inlines the values into the bundle** -- there is no
# runtime configuration to correct afterwards. A build made without an app id
# ships a site where sign-in is permanently dead, and it looks exactly like a
# working one until somebody tries to click it.
#
# VITE_FOMV_API is deliberately absent: `deploy/push-web.sh` sets it on the
# command line, because the origin is decided by where the build is being
# deployed rather than by a file that travels with the repo.

# Privy app id. Without it sign-in is unavailable and the rest of the site
# works, which is the intended degradation and not a good permanent state.
VITE_PRIVY_APP_ID=

# Session signer id, from the Privy dashboard under Wallet infrastructure.
# This app's wallets are TEE-backed, so authorisation is granted through
# session signers rather than the older delegated-actions API; the two are not
# interchangeable and the old one errors out.
VITE_PRIVY_SIGNER_ID=

# Calendly event link for the "Get listed" funnel. Without it an application is
# still recorded and the page says booking is unavailable rather than showing
# an empty box.
VITE_CALENDLY_URL=
